Subject: [PATCH] 894 (b), 2347: a reply that lists something comes out as
 Excel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lika's second phone file (16 Oct): „give me these three names as Excel"
got the names as text and no file. The only Excel that could leave Netai
was a worked uploaded list; a list Netai itself wrote had no way out.

GET /threads/:id/messages/:messageId/table.xlsx turns one shown assistant
reply into a one-sheet workbook: a Markdown table cell by cell, header
first, or a numbered or bulleted list of two or more items one per row. It
reads only a `kind = 'message'` assistant row of the caller's own thread,
so no step or engine turn leaves as a file. 404 when the reply lists
nothing. No model-facing text changes; the frontend contract is in
docs/FOR_FRONTEND.md.

